<BaseLayout title="Ideas & explorations" description="Open questions about scientific commercialization, judgment, AI, and practical tools. Early explorations by Anthony Maiorana.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="The notebook / Ideas & explorations" title="Questions worth following." description="Some questions are worth keeping around before they become a project. These are starting points for reading, conversations, and small experiments." />
  <section class="wrap section"><div class="narrow"><ul class="ideas-list">
    <li><p class="meta">01 / Research commercialization</p><h2>What should a scientist learn before building a company?</h2><p>Which commercial assumptions can be tested early, cheaply, and without losing sight of the science? The Lean Lab is the written starting point; a small toolkit is one possible next step.</p><p style="margin-top:15px"><a class="text-link" href="/projects/lean-lab-toolkit/">Explore the toolkit idea <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></p></li>
    <li><p class="meta">02 / AI & judgment</p><h2>When producing an answer gets easier, what makes it trustworthy?</h2><p>I’m interested in how people demonstrate capability, check evidence, and make decisions when AI can generate increasingly convincing work. The question applies to hiring, scientific work, and the tools we choose to trust.</p></li>
    <li><p class="meta">03 / Practical software</p><h2>What becomes possible when more people can build their own tools?</h2><p>AI-assisted development makes it worth trying smaller, more specific ideas. I want to understand where that helps someone do useful work—and where a spreadsheet or a clear explanation is already enough.</p></li>
  </ul><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Working on a related question? <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div></section>
